-- title:
--   Unramified sub-DVR A₀ of A with A=A₀[ζ_q]
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $\ell$ be a prime distinct from $q$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, equipped with an $L$-algebra structure exhibiting $L$ as its fraction field, such that the image of $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$, and suppose $\zeta_A \in A$ maps to $\zeta$ under $A \to L$. Let $K$ be any commutative $A$-algebra. The assertion is the existence of a commutative ring $A_0$ which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, together with algebra structures $A_0 \to A$ and $A_0 \to K$ making $A_0 \to A \to K$ a scalar tower, such that: the maximal ideal of $A_0$ is generated by $q$; the residue field of $A_0$ is finite; $A_0 \to A$ is injective; $A$ is a finite $A_0$-module; the images of $\ell$ and of $M'$ in $A_0$ are units; $A_0$ contains a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity; and $A_0[\zeta_A] = A$, i.e. the $A_0$-subalgebra of $A$ generated by $\zeta_A$ is the whole of $A$.
--
--   This produces the unramified coefficient ring $A_0$ underlying $A$ — unramifiedness being recorded in the form $\mathfrak{m}_{A_0} = (q)$ together with finiteness of the residue field — over which $A$ is generated by the $q$-th root of unity $\zeta_A$, with $\ell$, $M'$ invertible and a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity already present in $A_0$. It is used in the auxiliary level-one constructions for full-level modular curves, where the two theorems citing it identify adic completions of stalks and the action of level automorphisms over such a base.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevelOne_exists_unramified_subDVR_adjoin_eq_top_of_ne.lean

